 4. PREREQUISITES — HOW TO INSTALL / CONFIGURE
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

  (i) TEST_POSTGRES_URL
      Any PostgreSQL the local machine can reach. Example:
        postgres://postgres:aurelia-test-pw-9f3c2b@127.0.0.1:55432/aurelia_test
      The suites only create/drop their OWN scratch schemas
      (aurelia_test_api / aurelia_test_engine / aurelia_test_sched), so a
      real local Postgres is fine. Quickest local option:
        docker run -d --name pg-test -p 55432:5432 \
          -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=aurelia-test-pw-9f3c2b postgres:16
      Then: TEST_POSTGRES_URL=postgres://postgres:aurelia-test-pw-9f3c2b@127.0.0.1:55432/postgres
      Use a DISTINCTIVE password, not `postgres`: the API connectors suite
      asserts the literal password never appears in any response, and a
      response legitimately contains `"kind":"postgres"` (plus the database
      name when the URL path is /postgres), which trips that sentinel.

  (ii) .venv for python-export tests
      Create the venv in aerolexa-main and install the exact deps:
        cd aerolexa-main
        python3 -m venv .venv
        .venv/bin/pip install numpy scipy pandas scikit-learn nbformat
      (nbformat is REQUIRED — the ipynb tests call `nbformat.validate`.)

