 6. GOTCHAS LEARNED THIS SESSION (save you from re-discovering them)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

  * Never run the API suites without --testPathPattern='__tests__/api' —
    the global-setup boots the server only for that pattern.
  * Before an API run, kill stray dev servers or you get ECONNRESET /
    500s from a stale process fighting for the port:
        pkill -f 'next dev'; pkill -f 'next start'
  * Only the TEST process needs TEST_POSTGRES_URL exported; the dev
    server inherits env from global-setup (which spreads process.env),
    and the app itself connects using connector config received in the
    request body (credentials aren't read from the server env).
  * Full `npm test` (no pattern) is slow and mixes API (needs server)
    with unit — it gets aborted; prefer the targeted commands above.
  * The API connectors suite also asserts JSON responses parse correctly
    (getPgPassword() is now computed lazily — don't re-introduce a
    module-level `new URL(TEST_PG)` or the file crashes when unset).
  * Never run `pkill -f 'next dev'` from a shell whose own command line
    contains that string — pkill matches the shell itself and kills the
    run before Jest starts. Use `pkill -f '[n]ext dev'` instead.

